# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback.
# Real static files (and /assets/*) are served first and take precedence, and
# functions/_middleware.js runs ahead of this for every included route (proxy,
# slug-redirect, SEO injection). This rule only applies when the function calls
# next() and the static layer would otherwise 404 — i.e. a client-side route
# like /article/<slug> with no matching file — so the SPA shell (index.html) is
# returned with a 200 instead of a 404. Keeps SPA routing consistent on Pages.
/*    /index.html   200
